commit 68d0a831
author: cdvankammen
date: 2026-10-22 12:10:05 -0600
subject: feat(routing): per-model retry counts for fallback chains + custom node support in smart router

Backend work for the visual fallback rule builder (UI to follow):

1. handleComboChat now supports retriesPerModel (universal) and
   perModelRetries (per-model override map). On a retryable error, the SAME
   model is retried N times (with transient-error cooldown between attempts)
   before moving to the next model. Exceptions never retry (fail-fast to
   next model). Fallback chain entries carry attempt numbers.

2. settings.modelFallbacks accepts an advanced shape alongside the simple
   array form (backward compatible):
     Simple:   { target: ["fb1", "fb2"] }
     Advanced: { target: { models: [...], retries: N, perModelRetries: {...} } }
   chat.js normalizes both and wires retriesPerModel/perModelRetries into
   handleComboChat.

3. Smart router now scores user-defined provider nodes (custom
   OpenAI/Anthropic-compatible). getNodeModels() fetches the node's
   /models endpoint with a 5-min in-memory TTL cache and fails open ([]).
   Node candidates use the node PREFIX as the provider string so combos
   read like what clients type ("mockreal/gpt-4o-mini"). Respects
   allowedProviders (node id OR prefix) and allowedModels wildcards.

Tests: smart-router-resolve.test.js extended with custom-node eligibility
(fail-open) test — 8 total. Fallback-chain tests still pass with retry
param defaults (retriesPerModel=1 = unchanged behavior).

Refs: OpenRouter Auto Router cost/quality + allowed_models design
(https://openrouter.ai/docs/features/model-routing)


